## Prompt 1 - the master prompt 
```
ROLE: You are a senior front-end developer building a React web app.
GOAL:
Build the front end of RouteRelay, a logistics dispatch tool for internal dispatchers.
Their one job is:
“Move a late shipment to another driver and see the new arrival time.”
SCREENS:
Dispatch Board
Show at least 10 invented shipments with:
Shipment ID
Destination
Driver
ETA
Delay
Status
Status:
Green = On time
Red = Late
Amber = Reassigned
Late shipments should appear clearly in red.
Each late shipment has a “Reassign” button.
Reassign Shipment
When the user clicks Reassign, show:
Selected shipment
Current driver
Current ETA
Delay
Show 4–6 invented available drivers with:
Driver name
Vehicle number
Workload
New estimated arrival time
Let the dispatcher select one driver and press:
“Confirm Reassignment”
Updated Dispatch Board
Return to the Dispatch Board without reloading the page.
Update the selected shipment with:
New driver
New ETA
Status: Reassigned
Change the row from RED to AMBER.
The user knows it worked when:
“the row turns from red to amber.”
DATA:
Keep ALL invented data in ONE separate file.
Example:
src/data/logisticsData.js
Use only fictional:
shipment IDs
driver names
destinations
vehicle numbers
times
numbers
Include at least 10 shipment rows.
DESIGN:
Make it simple, clean, and mobile-friendly.
Use:
White/light grey background
Dark text
Red for late
Amber for reassigned
Green for on time
Large, readable buttons and text
Desktop can use a table.
Mobile should use simple cards.
SCOPE:
Front end only.
Do NOT:
call Gemini
call any AI model
call any outside service
fetch from any URL
use a database
create login
create accounts
use real company names or logos
add extra features
Use React state so screens change without reloading the page.
When finished, list the files created and what each file contains.
If you make a choice I did not specify, explain it in ONE short line.

